    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164847": {
      "title": "SMU Cox Adjunct Professor of Strategy",
      "description": "Department: Southern Methodist University: Cox School of Business Location: Dallas, TX Thank you for your interest in teaching at the Cox School of Business of Southern Methodist University in Dallas Texas. Per our faculty selection process, we typically set course schedules and make course staffing decisions a year in advance. Thus for the current and next year, most course staffing decisions have already been completed. Please review the Cox School course offerings http://www.smu.edu/catalogs and craft a short memo which indicates your teaching interest, what content you feel most comfortable with, specifically if you have past undergraduate and graduate teaching experiences, and it will be in this file for the department chairs to review. At this time we are not delivering  course material exclusively on-line. Teaching for the department requires a Ph.D. in a related field or 10  year of industry experience. Upload your resume and a memo with a list of classes previously taught, indicating your teaching interests."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185739": {
      "title": "SMU 26-27 - #05776 Energy - Clinical Professor or Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Department: Southern Methodist University: Cox School of Business Location: Dallas, TX SOUTHERN METHODIST UNIVERSITY Maguire Energy Institute, Cox School of Business Non-Tenure Track Position in Energy (Position Number: 005776) SMU invites applications for a non-tenure track full-time Professor of Practice position (005776) in the Maguire Energy Institute of SMU’s Cox School of Business, primarily supporting the new B.S. in Energy Science, Innovation, and Enterprise program. This is not a role focused on delivering an established curriculum — the Professor of Practice will help shape a new model for energy education, with the opportunity for lasting impact on students, the program, and the field. This is a contractual, non-tenure-track position for a minimum of three years, with the option for renewal, drawing from professionals with a focus on teaching and industry engagement. Salary is commensurate with experience. The Professor of Practice will serve as a cornerstone of a new, interdisciplinary honors degree program in Energy Science, Innovation, and Enterprise, reporting to the program’s Eminent Endowed Chair, with additional supervision by the Maguire Energy Institute. The successful candidate will lead project-based and experiential learning, organize on- and off-campus engagements connecting students with industry and government partners, bring applied case studies into the classroom, and serve as a liaison to local, state, and national opportunities for student internships and industry-sponsored projects. The role involves direct supervision of students during summer immersion experiences, in which students engage in real-world problem solving with cross-disciplinary teams and industry partners. In addition to teaching and experiential learning responsibilities, the Professor of Practice will help build and sustain partnerships with the Dallas–Fort Worth energy ecosystem and beyond, and will contribute to the program’s mission of preparing the next generation of energy leaders in the energy sector. Candidates are not expected to have expertise across every segment of the energy industry — we seek accomplished practitioners who bring deep expertise in one or more areas (such as energy finance, business, energy capture, systems engineering, policy and regulation, or technology commercialization) along with enthusiasm for working across disciplines. The position will begin in Fall 2027 with the option for a start date as early as January 2027. The Cox School is a nationally ranked business school located in Dallas, Texas, a premier business center in the U.S. The School offers a collegial working environment, attractive compensation and benefits, generous faculty support and outstanding facilities. Cox has just completed a $140 MM expansion and renovation project to create the David B Miller Quad (DBMQ), the new home of most of the faculty and staff, as well as many of the School’s programs. The Maguire Energy Institute serves as the hub for teaching and research in energy economics and finance, fostering collaboration between industry, academia, and policy communities through symposia, joint research initiatives, and partnerships across the Cox School of Business, the Lyle School of Engineering, and Dedman College of Humanities and Sciences. The Energy Science, Innovation, and Enterprise Program is an innovative, interdisciplinary honors degree program operated through the Office of the Provost, designed to produce graduates ready to lead across the full spectrum of energy—from oil and gas and renewable energy to energy finance, policy, infrastructure, and technology commercialization. The program brings together SMU’s Cox School of Business, Lyle School of Engineering, and Dedman College of Humanities and Sciences, providing students with both theoretical foundations and deep applied experience in partnership with the Dallas–Fort Worth energy community and beyond. SMU is a private university dedicated to academic excellence. Located in Dallas, SMU maintains a moderate size of about 12,000 students. SMU is designated as a preferred employer offering in the Dallas/Fort Worth metroplex, one of the most prolific high-tech industrial and business centers in the country. The Dallas/Fort Worth metroplex is a multi-faceted business community, offering exceptional museums, diverse cultural attractions and one of the fastest-growing and most vibrant economies in the USA. Dallas’ quality of life is exceptional with a relatively low cost of living, upscale apartments and homes within walking distance of campus, the opportunity to live in the city or out in the country with a relatively short commute, and the availability of mass transit systems. Minimum qualifications: A graduate degree (master’s or higher) in Energy, Finance, Economics, or a related field (a J.D. is an acceptable equivalent qualifying degree); demonstrated teaching, training, mentoring, or educational experience (university teaching experience preferred but not required); and substantial, demonstrated experience in the energy industry. Preferred qualifications: An advanced degree (Ph.D. or professional equivalent) in Energy, Finance, Economics, or a related field; five or more years of experience in the energy industry; university teaching experience, particularly innovative, experiential teaching; demonstrated success in building industry partnerships and facilitating applied, project-based learning; and a professional network in the energy sector, particularly in oil and gas, renewable energy, energy finance, or energy policy. Application: Applicants should provide a cover letter that describes relevant teaching and industry experience in energy, curriculum vitae, three letters of reference, or names and contact information for three references, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Priority will be given to applications received by October 15, 2026, although the committee will continue to accept applications until the position is filled. The recruiting committee, along with other interested parties, will conduct initial interviews through Zoom. Hiring is contingent on the satisfactory completion of a background check."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191583": {
      "title": "SMU 26-27 - #1404 Associate or Full Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Department: Southern Methodist University: Cox School of Business Location: Dallas  SOUTHERN METHODIST UNIVERSITY Cox School of Business Associate or Full Professor in Finance #01404 SMU's Cox School of Business invites applications for tenure/tenure-track position at the Associate or Full Professor level in the Finance Department. This search comes at a pivotal moment for the department, college, and university, as we invest to further strengthen the group; the successful candidate will have a genuine opportunity to help shape its future direction. Endowed positions are also possible. Applications from associate and full professors should demonstrate established post-tenure achievements and a robust pipeline of ongoing research. In the rare case, we will consider advanced assistant candidates. Both salary and teaching load are competitive, as is support for research and instruction. Faculty will be expected to produce high-quality research, participate in university service, and to deliver high-quality instruction in courses across the School's undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs, which include online teaching. The position will begin Fall 2027. Hiring is contingent on the satisfactory completion of a background check. The Finance Department has 18 tenure-track/tenured research faculty who publish in top academic journals, participate in national and international conferences, collaborate with scholars across the globe, and inform policy debates. The Department also has excellent teaching faculty whose effectiveness in the classroom contributes to an outstanding student experience. The Department has excellent relationships with the corporate and business community, which helps provide a compelling environment for both research and teaching. Further information about the Finance Department at SMU can be found at https://www.smu.edu/cox/academics/finance-department The Cox School is a nationally ranked business school located in Dallas, Texas, home to 24 Fortune 500 headquarters, a burgeoning financial sector nicknamed 'Y'all Street,' and a pro-business climate featuring no state income tax. The School offers a collegial working environment, attractive compensation and benefits, generous faculty support and outstanding facilities. The School recently completed a $140 million expansion and renovation project to create the new David B. Miller Business Quadrangle, the new home of most of the Cox faculty and staff, as well as many of our programs. For more information about the facilities, visit: https://www.dallasnews.com/fwddfw/2024/05/03/new-home-for-smu-cox-school-of-business-will-prepare-future-leaders-and-benefit-dallas SMU is a private university dedicated to academic excellence. Located in Dallas, SMU maintains a moderate size of about 12,000 students. SMU is designated as a preferred employer in the Dallas/Fort Worth metroplex, one of the most prolific high-tech industrial and business centers in the country, and a region well-suited to dual-career couples given the concentration of universities nearby, including the Dallas Fed, TCU, UTD, UTA, UNT, and Baylor. Dallas' quality of life is exceptional, with a relatively low cost of living, upscale apartments and homes within walking distance of campus, the opportunity to live in the city or out in the country with a relatively short commute, and the availability of both mass transit systems and plentiful on-campus parking. Minimum qualifications: Ph.D. in Finance or Economics, exhibit promise for high-quality research and teaching. Preferred qualifications: Applicants should have an established publication record in top-tier academic journals, a strong working research pipeline, substantial teaching experience and demonstrated excellence, a record of professional service and leadership in the field and promise for continued high-quality research and teaching. Application: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until hiring is complete, with priority given to applications received by October 1, 2026. Applicants should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, examples of written work, three names of references to be contacted for letters before any offer can be made, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. The Finance faculty will conduct initial interviews through Zoom. Any questions or inquiries may be directed to the Finance Department administrative assistant Christina Elmore at christinae@smu.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191584": {
      "title": "SMU 26-27 - #49928 Associate or Full Professor in ITOM",
      "description": "Department: Southern Methodist University: Cox School of Business Location: Dallas SOUTHERN METHODIST UNIVERSITY Cox School of Business Tenure Track Faculty Position in Associate or Full Tenured Faculty Position in Information Technology and Operations Management # 49928 SMU’s Cox School of Business invites applications for tenured positions at the Associate or Full Professor level in the Information Technology and Operations Management (ITOM) Department. Endowed positions are also possible. All candidates should demonstrate established post-tenure achievements and a robust pipeline of ongoing research. Both salary and teaching load are competitive, as is support for research and instruction. Faculty will be expected to conduct high-quality research, participate in university service, and to deliver high-quality instruction in courses across undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs, which include online teaching. The position will begin August 2027. The Cox School is a nationally ranked business school located in Dallas, Texas, a premier business center in the U.S. The School offers a collegial working environment, generous faculty support and outstanding facilities.  The Information Technology and Operations Management Department has well-respected research faculty, who actively publish in top academic journals, participate in national and international conferences, collaborate with scholars across the globe, and inform policy debates on topics such as Information Systems Design and Supply Chain Management. The department has excellent relations with the corporate and business community and has an advisory board of senior executives of leading companies, providing a unique and exciting environment for both teaching and research. Further information about the ITOM department can be found at https://www.smu.edu/cox/academics/information-technology-and-operations-management-department SMU is a private university dedicated to academic excellence. Located in Dallas, SMU maintains a moderate size of about 12,000 students. SMU is designated as a preferred employer in the Dallas/Fort Worth metroplex, one of the most prolific high-tech industrial and business centers in the country, and a region well-suited to dual-career couples given the concentration of universities nearby, including TCU, UTD, UTA, and Baylor. Dallas' quality of life is exceptional, with a relatively low cost of living, upscale apartments and homes within walking distance of campus, the opportunity to live in the city or out in the country with a relatively short commute, and the availability of both mass transit systems and plentiful on-campus parking. Minimum qualifications: Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree) in Information Systems, Business Analytics and/or Operations Management or a related field; demonstrated track record of high-quality research and teaching . Preferred qualifications: A research focus in artificial intelligence, data and analytics, cybersecurity and privacy, digital platforms, or technology-enabled operations and supply chains is desired. Applicants should have an established publication record in top-tier academic journals, strong working research pipeline, demonstrated excellence in teaching, and a record of professional service and leadership in the field. Application: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until hiring is complete, with priority given to applications received by October 1, 2026. Applicants should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, examples of written work, three names of references for letters to be contacted before an offer is made, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. The ITOM faculty will conduct initial interviews at the INFORMS Annual Meeting in Oct-Nov 2026, as well as virtually through Zoom. Hiring is contingent on the satisfactory completion of a background check.  Any questions or inquiries may be directed to the ITOM administrative assistant Jill McGinness jmcginness@smu.edu or department chair Sree Bhaskaran at sbhaskar@smu.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191586": {
